<title>CHINA: HK bourse says 33 listing applications in process.</title>
<headline>HK bourse says 33 listing applications in process.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Ltd said  it was processing a total of 33 applications for share listings in  Hong Kong as at July 31, 1997.</p>
<p>All 33 companies have submitted advance booking forms for equity and  debt securities (A1 forms) and furnished all required and necessary  information, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>A further five companies have been approved by the listing committee  of the exchange but were not yet listed, it said.</p>
<p>Another two companies have submitted A1 forms but their cases were  either inactive or on-hold, it added.</p>
<p>The exchange said it also received preliminary enquiries from 13 companies  but A1 forms were not yet submitted.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
